  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 235 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nToday through Sunday...Troughing will slowly advance east across the \nDeep South while gradually weakening through mid-week.  This will \nallow high pressure aloft to strengthen across the Lower Mississippi \nRiver Valley during the mid and latter portion of the forecast \nperiod.  As a result, the weather across the forecast area will \nremain rather quiet, with rain chances coming in the form of \ndiurnally driven isolated showers and storms, mainly late in the \nweek and into the upcoming weekend.\n\nAs far as impactful weather during the forecast period, this will \nagain come in the form of increasing heat stress, mainly from \nThursday through Sunday.  The slightly drier air currently residing \nacross the CWA was been a nice and welcomed relief from the \noppressively humid conditions over the past week.  Unfortunately \nthrough the week, moisture will gradually increase as dew points \nclimb back well into the 70s areawide heading into the weekend. \nThis, as high temperatures climb back into at least the middle 90s, \nwill yield afternoon heat index values approaching levels where \nmultiple days of perhaps a \"Heat Advisory\" will need to be hoisted \nfor portions of, if not all of, the forecast area during the \nThursday through Sunday timeframe.  This will continue to be \nmonitored in future forecasts. /19/",
